import theorem.GridTiedConverter.GFM.FullModel.BoundaryLayerRouth
import theorem.Dynamics.PolyIdentity

/-! # The 13-state grid-forming converter: the boundary layer of the ideal design in closed form

Model boundary.
The ten-state fast block `fastBlock δ` of
`theorem/GridTiedConverter/GFM/FullModel/BoundaryLayer.lean` (filter current, capacitor voltage,
line current, current- and voltage-loop integrators, dq, linearized in the fast states; the real
form of the complex `5 × 5` matrix `fastMatrix δ`) in the ideal design: full current
feed-forward `k_ff = 1`, full decoupling `k_dv = 1`, no virtual impedance `Z_v = 0`; every other
parameter value with `L_f, C_f, L_g ≠ 0` (any signs of gains and resistances). Normalized
parameters as in `theorem/GridTiedConverter/GFM/FullModel/BoundaryLayerRouth.lean`:
`k_p = K_pc/L_f`, `k_i = K_ic/L_f`, `ρ = R_f/L_f`, `r = R_g/L_g`, `w = ω₀`, `c = 1/(C_f L_g)`,
`P = K_pv/C_f`, `q = K_iv/C_f` (and `e = κ = r_v = x_v = 0`). Continuous time, constant
matrices; excluded: everything excluded by the boundary layer of the full-order model. The last
determinant `Δ₁₀` is in `theorem/GridTiedConverter/GFM/FullModel/BoundaryLayerIdealDelta10.lean`.

Source: GFM counterpart study, full-order model note (t5: the boundary layer); the complex
Routh–Hurwitz criterion of H. Bilharz, *Z. Angew. Math. Mech.* 24 (1944)
(`theorem/Criteria/Bilharz.lean`). The determinants were expanded by exact computer algebra
(discovery evidence) and are checked here by the kernel through the reflective
polynomial-identity check of `theorem/Dynamics/PolyIdentity.lean` (`poly_rfl`), after rewriting
the Bilharz polynomials into Horner form (a proof device that shortens the expansion).

Results.
* In the ideal design the voltage-level cubic factors, `χ_v(s) = (s + r + jw)(s² + P s + q)`
  (the coefficients `FastLevel.coeffs kp ki ρ r w c P 0 q 0 0 0`), and the third and fourth
  Bilharz determinants of the boundary layer are the explicit polynomials `IdealLevel.delta6`
  (398 terms) and `IdealLevel.delta8` (2922 terms, three parts) of `k_p, k_i, ρ, r, w, c, P, q`
  (`IdealLevel.quinticBilharz6_eq`, `IdealLevel.quinticBilharz8_eq`); both are irreducible over
  `ℚ`, even in `w`, with 143 and 1285 negative coefficients, so they carry no sign law of their
  own.
* `Params.fastDelta_two_ideal`, `Params.fastDelta_three_ideal`: the determinants of the
  parameter set; **`Params.spectrallyStable_fastBlock_iff_ideal`**: the boundary layer of the
  ideal design is spectrally stable iff `k_p + ρ + r > 0`, `FastLevel.delta4 > 0` (at
  `e = κ = r_v = x_v = 0`), `IdealLevel.delta6 > 0`, `IdealLevel.delta8 > 0` and `Δ₁₀ > 0`.
-/

noncomputable section
namespace powerlib.GFM.FullModel

namespace IdealLevel

